          "B": "2",
          "C": "1",
          "D": "0"
        },
        "source_answer": "A",
        "source_answer_status": "PRESENT",
        "independent_derivation": "f(1) = 1 - 8 + 20 - 13 = 0, so (x-1) is a factor. Division gives f(x) = (x-1)(x^2 - 7x + 13). For f(x) to be prime, either x - 1 = 1 (x=2 => f(2)=3 prime), x - 1 = -1 (x=0 not positive), or x^2 - 7x + 13 = 1 => (x-3)(x-4)=0 => x=3 (f(3)=2 prime), x=4 (f(4)=3 prime). Admissible positive integers are x in {2, 3, 4}, count = 3.",
